message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software archive and the associated article below."
title: "Casimir-Electrostatic NEMS Pull-In: Bifurcation, Phase Diagrams & Physics-Informed Neural Networks"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible computational archive for the study of the pull-in instability of
  a Casimir-electrostatic nano-electromechanical (NEMS) oscillator. It derives the
  closed-form saddle-node (fold) bifurcation of the pull-in boundary, maps the
  dynamic pull-in phase diagram by deterministic Runge-Kutta integration, trains
  physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) that solve the governing ODE including a
  pull-in-safe rapidity parametrization for the movable pole and a parametric PINN
  that learns the fold boundary from the force-balance residual, and computes the
  finite-temperature Lifshitz shift of the pull-in voltage.
